                'en' => 'The BEA-TT gives two direct causes: a misjudgement of the convoy\'s clearance and of the effect of the humpbacked road profile, hence the snagging of the gantry; then an inadequate reaction by the staff, who stopped the convoy on the tracks when nothing prevented them from clearing them. Among the factors it cites the failure to request authorisation for the final leg, the lack of contact with SNCF, a team disorganised by the departure that same morning of the most experienced driver, and ignorance of the risks of stopping on a level crossing.',
